.\" Visage — System Performance Dashboard
.TH VISAGE 1 "2026-08-20" "Visage 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
visage \- system performance dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B visage
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Visage
is a real-time system performance dashboard for Linux, providing live monitoring of CPU, memory, disk, network, GPU, sensors, and processes in a beautiful terminal UI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-benchmark
Run CPU, memory, and disk benchmarks.
.TP
.BR "\-\-remote"
Start the remote monitoring HTTP server (default port 8090).
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-port " PORT"
Remote server port (default: 8090).
.TP
.BR \-\-export
Snapshot metrics once to JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-export\-continuous
Continuous CSV export at regular intervals.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-interval " SECS"
Interval in seconds for continuous export (default: 5.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Output path for \-\-export (default: visage_snapshot.json).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to config JSON file.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q
Quit the dashboard.
.TP
.B r
Force refresh all metrics.
.TP
.B d
Cycle refresh speed (0.5s, 1s, 2s, 5s).
.TP
.B t
Cycle through color themes.
.TP
.B s
Sort process table (CPU, Memory, PID, Name).
.TP
.B a
Toggle aggregate mode (group by process name).
.TP
.B t
Toggle tree view for processes.
.TP
.B v
Toggle vim keybinding mode.
.TP
.B l
Toggle long command line display.
.TP
.B n
Renice selected process.
.TP
.B /
Filter processes by name.
.TP
.B Enter
Open/close process detail panel.
.TP
.B Esc
Close popups and vim mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I visage.json
Local configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/visage/config.json
User configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B visage
Start the live dashboard.
.TP
.B visage \-\-remote \-\-remote\-port 9090
Start remote server on port 9090.
.TP
.B visage \-\-export \-\-output metrics.json
Export a single metrics snapshot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR htop (1),
.BR btop (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR vmstat (8)
